statement:
Let $i:Z\to X$ be a closed immersion of schemes [def-weil-closed-immersion] [def-pc-scheme]. Then:
(a) $i$ is proper (separated, of finite type and universally closed) [def-weil-proper-morphism];
(b) for every proper morphism of schemes $f:X\to S$ [def-weil-proper-morphism], the composite $f\circ i:Z\to S$ is proper;
(c) in particular, if $X$ is a scheme proper over a scheme $S$ and $Z\subseteq X$ is a closed subscheme, i.e. $Z$ comes with a closed immersion $i:Z\to X$, then $Z$ is proper over $S$ (its structure morphism $Z\to X\to S$ is proper).
